# LeoVer regression Definition of Done

A change is **not done** if related tests are missing, stale, or not run.

Daily default is **lightweight**. Do **not** start LeoVer-QA or Maestro unless the user explicitly asks (`-Maestro`, `-SmokeE2E`, `-FullE2E`).

## Before declaring done

1. Name the behavior that changed.
2. Find or add the cheapest tests that protect it (unit / contract / ViewModel / SQL-RPC / RLS).
3. Run `.\scripts\qa\run-regression.ps1 -Affected` (defaults to Fast; no emulator).
4. Report results. Never claim PASS from inspection only.

## Layer

| Change | Minimum tests | Maestro |
| --- | --- | --- |
| New feature | New tests + affected Fast suite | Only if user-visible Android path cannot be proven cheaper |
| Modified behavior | Review/update existing tests | Same |
| Bugfix | Failing cheap test first, then fix | Do **not** make every bug a Maestro flow |
| Migration / RPC | Contract + security/RLS if ACL/data | No auto E2E |
| UI behavior | Unit/contract/Compose-without-device | `MAESTRO_REQUIRED: YES` if E2E needed, **do not start it** |
| Visual only | `UiRegressionGateTest` / screenshot note | MANUAL if hardware |

## Report every implementation

```
TEST IMPACT: ...
FAST/AFFECTED TESTS: PASS | FAIL | NOT RUN
MAESTRO REQUIRED: YES | NO
MAESTRO RUN: NOT RUN | PASS | FAIL
FULL REGRESSION: NOT RUN
```

If tests were not executed, write **NOT RUN**. Never write "implemented" without this block.

## Catalog

Map rules in `docs/qa/regression-catalog.yaml`. Use `docs/qa/change-impact-map.yaml` to pick suites. Gate: `scripts/qa/check-regression-coverage.ps1`.

## Forbidden as daily default

- Auto-start emulator or Maestro
- Full E2E on every change
- Personal phone as QA target
- Declaring FULL PASS when security tests failed
